# Local env for cron-agent. Plain KEY=value lines only, no quotes, no comments on values.
# Never commit this file. Copy from .env.example handling.
# Precedence: `make VAR=x` beats this file, this file beats Makefile defaults.
# Shipped binary: place a copy named .env next to the binary, or pass --env <path>.
# The binary also reads ./.env from its working dir. Exported env vars always win.

# Server port. Leave commented for default 8080.
# PORT=8080

# Data dir, relative to repo root or absolute. Leave commented for ./data.
# DATA_DIR=./data

# Bearer token guarding POST endpoints (trigger, pause, resume). Leave empty for local dev.
# Set a real value before exposing the server anywhere.
# API_TOKEN=
